    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 167,
        "text": "Hi, everyone. Thanks for coming to our project meeting. We need to choose a method for our small research project on student study habits. Let's start with ideas.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "464d11c1cb0e65f99b2da6a9105f4368487882edaab26f8b0b65bf6ca09d6614",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 174,
        "sourceEnd": 386,
        "text": "I think we should use a questionnaire. It's fast, and we can get many answers. Because of the large number of students, a questionnaire is practical. It allows us to collect data from many people in a short time.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b47f2c8be59373713da87fe2454a37ce7cbb2991c391386bf68e2e1ec91c90f8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 393,
        "sourceEnd": 576,
        "text": "That's true. Although a questionnaire is quick, the answers may be short. We might not learn why students study in certain ways. We need to understand the reasons behind their habits.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0955d9e1dfb65ca41ad45c3d1328e7757f30abecae68fe77309b0855607bd06c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 583,
        "sourceEnd": 752,
        "text": "Right. But we can add some open questions. While closed questions are easy to count, open questions give more detail. This way, we can get both numbers and explanations.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d698bcf4611ce2b8e3b13b3a44e25081116c352ece13f1a274066dc69ad53aeb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 759,
        "sourceEnd": 793,
        "text": "Good point. What about interviews?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "dcd84c9bf6d69a783e6da03e2007976b38d692cf5c77f2b88392164e8c6b15b8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "sara",
        "speaker": "Sara",
        "sourceStart": 801,
        "sourceEnd": 1002,
        "text": "Interviews are useful because we can ask follow-up questions. But they take a lot of time. Because of the time limit, we can only interview a few students. We have only two weeks for the whole project.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "37ebb2db644472e4cdb5021d045314cc09813f7e9b6bd343213ddf98a97f1691",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1009,
        "sourceEnd": 1171,
        "text": "So, maybe we combine both? A short questionnaire for many students, and a few interviews for deeper information. This mixed method could give us a fuller picture.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "997698bac9e79676399d168e909e1d796db580ee621222fdf08bb168db94dbc7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1178,
        "sourceEnd": 1317,
        "text": "I like that. Although it needs more planning, it gives us both width and depth. We can reach many students and still explore their reasons.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "e689c54755d8114e634a8880c215c5c40922b1be17e624d84f088cd3c81bee66",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "sara",
        "speaker": "Sara",
        "sourceStart": 1325,
        "sourceEnd": 1516,
        "text": "Yes. While the questionnaire gives us numbers, the interviews give us stories. Because we have two weeks, we should start the questionnaire this week. Then we can do the interviews next week.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "e9badb4627436ec2eef728ddf5f8919edc0a34eb6509cf3c71097c2c472fb4c0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1523,
        "sourceEnd": 1636,
        "text": "OK. Let's decide: questionnaire first, then interviews with five volunteers. Sara, can you prepare the questions?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a0f2a3aa5931369ff4c7a6d13aecca086d801934eccc6ec8feabf00f09228316",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "sara",
        "speaker": "Sara",
        "sourceStart": 1644,
        "sourceEnd": 1728,
        "text": "Sure. I'll send a draft by Friday. I'll make sure the questions are clear and short.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "c9f73cc02ef2196ca42cec879f807b528c0fba7e69c46e293837c3c52fb06020",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1735,
        "sourceEnd": 1871,
        "text": "And I'll check the questionnaire for clear language. I'll also make sure the questions are not too difficult for students to understand.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "84d18ce6509ae23cf4b960ed112a1703329e8b2283ccff20ea08bb55442d2c90",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1878,
        "sourceEnd": 1952,
        "text": "Great. Thanks, everyone. Let's meet again next Monday to review the draft.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "d650b8b4645a507bf62b51d38408aa7cd9216e9e4f034a773aa2070dbb84da18",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      }
    ]
  },
